The remove-then-add sequence exists as described: ensureCityOverlay removes the old layers before building L.imageOverlay(reg.url) and washMake, and Leaflet's _initImage gives each new layer a new <img src=data:...>. The redundant double wash is real, but only inside the hot-swap path. The deciding facts are the order in worldCityUpdate (ensureCityGen before ensureCityOverlay((reg&&z>6.5)?...:null)) and the CITYVIEW.name===key checks in registerCityOverlay and washRefresh. Together they mean an ordinary first zoom into an invented city never hot-swaps: the plan simply appears for the first time. The real cases are narrower:
- flyIntoCity into an unsampled invented city (synthetic plan, then a melded swap during the fly, usually below the z6.8 fade-in);
- the canon cities' one-time wash re-tone;
- LRU evictions after 6 more-recent cities (a cache hit re-uses the same img).
The blank frame itself is unverified and depends on how each browser decodes images. Because the stated trigger is wrong and the effect is rare and unmeasured, holds is false and the severity is minor.

