votes.reason:
The quoted evidence is accurate. In docs/mobile/units.json, A-U3 says "glyphs never move (no badge offset): marker glyph rects equal R1" and A-U4 says "marker glyph rects equal R1". The faction-spread line in buildFactionBadges is quoted verbatim, and it offsets only n>=1, so the first badge sits on the seat. A2 in inputs.json is the Lektān badge stacked on Epēshu, and A-U3 resolves it by tap distance, not by an offset. So "fixes that move glyphs conflict with A-U3/A-U4" holds for any change made inside a mobile unit.

applies_to_us ("can only land after G9") is wrong as stated. docs/mobile/README.md lets non-mobile commits change an app file mid-lane, provided no atlas unit holds the file and references are rebased before the next unit ("Traced road network ... if it lands mid-lane, references are rebased"; "a rebase whenever a non-mobile commit changes an app file mid-lane"). G9 is also not a free-for-all afterwards. It records the maps-site sha as the Filigree 2 baseline, and later changes trigger the rebase rule. The real constraints are three:
- never inside a mobile unit;
- a rebase plus a tap-fixture re-run whenever glyphs move;
- an explicit decision to supersede A-U3's "no badge offset" for the faction spread.

The best slot is after G9 and before Filigree 2's baseline, or inside filigree slice B. The names of the four fixes are not in the repo; they come from the gap lens, so I took them as named.

prior_record.claim:
Whatever replaces cityBox has to be ONE transform used in both directions. POI markers (buildWorldPOIs, worldPOICoord) and the wash (washMake) all derive their geometry from cityBox. Road stubs (buildCityStubs) do not: they are drawn from reg.stubs, already in world px, with no box mapping. With a Helmert or affine registration:
- art px to world: the forward transform places POIs and any vector city vertices;
- the raster gets the inverse, or is pre-warped by the same parameters;
- wash and bounds use the transformed quad.
Without this, POIs float off the art. Because washMake is hash-pinned, changed geometry should reach it through reg/a fields and not by editing its body.

